1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:22,160
guys fall is here you're excited yeah yeah yeah yeah yeah yeah we weather the swimming crisis

2
00:00:22,160 --> 00:00:27,680
over summer only for an autumn challenge to rear its ugly head i'm aware it sucks

3
00:00:27,680 --> 00:00:36,080
are they holding a week over there the party's here and he has his class's sports day team assignments

4
00:00:36,080 --> 00:00:42,720
oh yeah oh wait do i not hand them off to you guys or no you do

5
00:00:46,080 --> 00:00:51,200
feels as if sports day creeps closer and closer every time a class turns in a form hate to break

6
00:00:51,200 --> 00:00:53,680
it to you pal but it is getting closer every time

7
00:00:57,680 --> 00:01:03,840
uh let's pray for a raid let's do a rain dance

8
00:01:06,880 --> 00:01:10,720
hey everyone our roster's ready what's going on

9
00:01:10,720 --> 00:01:19,920
is

10
00:01:20,800 --> 00:01:25,120
is

11
00:01:29,120 --> 00:01:31,840
we

12
00:01:31,840 --> 00:02:01,820
Thank you.

13
00:02:01,840 --> 00:02:31,820
Thank you.

14
00:02:31,840 --> 00:02:33,840
Thank you.

15
00:03:01,840 --> 00:03:03,840
Thank you.

16
00:03:32,840 --> 00:03:34,500
Okay. Good luck to you.

17
00:03:34,720 --> 00:03:36,060
I said our dust.

18
00:03:37,060 --> 00:03:39,340
Iyorta and Yuki are also on the East team.

19
00:03:39,760 --> 00:03:41,600
You're kidding me.

20
00:03:42,380 --> 00:03:43,820
Those gung-ho teammates.

21
00:03:43,940 --> 00:03:46,920
No way am I going to be able to stay out of sight and do nothing.

22
00:03:47,340 --> 00:03:50,100
Such a loaded confession, yet spoken so casually.

23
00:03:51,080 --> 00:03:54,200
I thought he was absent, but he was just slacking off.

24
00:03:54,580 --> 00:03:57,420
Oh, the girls are performing a cheer routine, right?

25
00:03:58,420 --> 00:04:00,800
Will you be cheering too, Sakura?

26
00:04:00,800 --> 00:04:02,720
Will I cheer?

27
00:04:03,560 --> 00:04:05,520
Yes, I will.

28
00:04:05,920 --> 00:04:09,820
Even if we possess no sense of rhythm at all, it's mandatory.

29
00:04:11,040 --> 00:04:13,420
Hey, your voice went down a few octaves.

30
00:04:13,840 --> 00:04:15,400
Gotta make our pom-poms, yeah?

31
00:04:15,940 --> 00:04:16,500
Indeed.

32
00:04:17,200 --> 00:04:18,860
I hope our routine isn't too hard.

33
00:04:19,580 --> 00:04:21,800
I haven't even asked if you're East or West.

34
00:04:22,220 --> 00:04:23,160
West, thankfully.

35
00:04:23,780 --> 00:04:24,520
Remy is too.

36
00:04:25,060 --> 00:04:26,260
Meaning we'll be rivals.

37
00:04:26,640 --> 00:04:28,260
At least you'll have Toru and Miyamura.

38
00:04:28,260 --> 00:04:32,260
I'm on the same team as Ishikawa.

39
00:04:36,220 --> 00:04:39,400
And he's going to see me out there flailing like an idiot!

40
00:04:40,780 --> 00:04:43,120
Can rhythmless people rain dance, you think?

41
00:04:43,220 --> 00:04:43,540
Yes!

42
00:04:43,700 --> 00:04:44,780
Come and sit with me!

43
00:04:46,300 --> 00:04:47,140
Rain dance!

44
00:04:47,300 --> 00:04:48,040
Rain dance!

45
00:04:48,240 --> 00:04:49,840
Is the student council okay?

46
00:04:50,120 --> 00:04:50,880
Rain dance!

47
00:04:53,000 --> 00:04:54,140
What's his deal?

48
00:04:54,680 --> 00:04:57,640
I mean, the guy's been a klutz since we were little kids, sure.

49
00:04:58,260 --> 00:05:01,720
But as our student council president, he has got to suck it up!

50
00:05:02,120 --> 00:05:05,520
So I take it his clumsiness didn't make him much of an athlete, huh?

51
00:05:05,720 --> 00:05:06,620
Not at all.

52
00:05:06,760 --> 00:05:08,360
Always crying and falling down.

53
00:05:09,360 --> 00:05:12,000
It'd be nice if he could take a page out of Sota's book.

54
00:05:13,080 --> 00:05:14,080
You think?

55
00:05:14,760 --> 00:05:16,740
Because I, uh...

56
00:05:16,740 --> 00:05:17,080
Hmm.

57
00:05:17,980 --> 00:05:21,600
I don't have any good sports day memories either, so I sympathize.

58
00:05:21,600 --> 00:05:21,820
Hmm?

59
00:05:25,320 --> 00:05:28,980
You're lightning on your feet, which makes you a great competitor for the hundred meter!

60
00:05:30,060 --> 00:05:31,360
Don't get me, bleh!

61
00:05:32,020 --> 00:05:34,080
What you should be giving is your all!

62
00:05:35,520 --> 00:05:37,760
Because I intend to give it the exact same.

63
00:05:37,940 --> 00:05:40,340
So absolutely zero slacking or else!

64
00:05:40,340 --> 00:05:45,380
As far as sports go, I'm really not that gifted either.

65
00:05:45,740 --> 00:05:47,460
But I think I'll surpass last year.

66
00:05:48,060 --> 00:05:48,740
Call it a hunch.

67
00:05:50,900 --> 00:05:53,520
You honestly want me to go all out in that race?

68
00:05:53,740 --> 00:05:54,360
Mm-hmm.

69
00:05:54,820 --> 00:05:57,220
And you want me to cheer when I'm on the sidelines?

70
00:05:57,540 --> 00:05:58,480
Yep, that's right!

71
00:05:59,120 --> 00:06:01,480
Then when I take the field, will you cheer for me?

72
00:06:01,960 --> 00:06:03,500
Of course I will, duh!

73
00:06:04,120 --> 00:06:05,700
We're on different teams, though.

74
00:06:06,420 --> 00:06:08,820
Well, yeah, I know that.

75
00:06:08,820 --> 00:06:11,920
But I'll still be watching.

76
00:06:14,200 --> 00:06:14,680
Right.

77
00:06:15,920 --> 00:06:16,820
How strange.

78
00:06:17,660 --> 00:06:20,320
I wanted it to be over as soon as possible before.

79
00:06:21,360 --> 00:06:23,580
But now I'm genuinely looking forward to it.

80
00:06:25,300 --> 00:06:26,440
Yo, Miyamura!

81
00:06:27,060 --> 00:06:28,180
Can I swing by tomorrow night?

82
00:06:28,680 --> 00:06:29,660
Sorry, but no.

83
00:06:30,080 --> 00:06:31,340
Gotta prep for sports day.

84
00:06:32,080 --> 00:06:32,460
Really?

85
00:06:33,020 --> 00:06:35,340
My school held our sports day back in June.

86
00:06:35,900 --> 00:06:36,840
What events are you doing?

87
00:06:37,180 --> 00:06:38,300
Or are you skipping?

88
00:06:38,820 --> 00:06:42,780
I'm still debating, but I might do the 100-meter dash.

89
00:06:43,480 --> 00:06:44,000
Maybe.

90
00:06:44,540 --> 00:06:45,060
Oh.

91
00:06:46,100 --> 00:06:47,640
Someone sounds motivated.

92
00:06:48,740 --> 00:06:49,140
Yeah.

93
00:06:50,080 --> 00:06:51,280
Surprisingly, I am.

94
00:06:52,340 --> 00:06:53,900
Wow, cool.

95
00:06:54,640 --> 00:06:56,920
Might have to come see this passion firsthand.

96
00:06:57,360 --> 00:06:58,420
No, don't you dare.

97
00:06:58,420 --> 00:07:02,500
I'd be willing to bet anything.

98
00:07:02,500 --> 00:07:06,120
The days ahead will be a bit crazier than usual.

99
00:07:08,200 --> 00:07:09,560
That's it for today, girls.

100
00:07:09,940 --> 00:07:10,620
Good work!

101
00:07:13,820 --> 00:07:15,140
It's so hard.

102
00:07:15,140 --> 00:07:19,120
I'm the only one having trouble with the moves.

103
00:07:19,120 --> 00:07:22,360
I'll be as humiliated as I was last sports day.

104
00:07:22,760 --> 00:07:23,760
Maybe more.

105
00:07:24,840 --> 00:07:28,460
Because this year, Ishikawa could see me make a fool of myself.

106
00:07:28,460 --> 00:07:31,340
Hey there, Kono.

107
00:07:33,080 --> 00:07:33,520
Yoshikawa.

108
00:07:33,520 --> 00:07:35,320
Are you all right?

109
00:07:35,980 --> 00:07:37,640
You aren't feeling sick, are you?

110
00:07:37,700 --> 00:07:39,060
No, that's not it.

111
00:07:39,760 --> 00:07:41,420
Okay, then what's wrong?

112
00:07:42,300 --> 00:07:44,840
Guess I'm wiped from practicing our cheer routine.

113
00:07:45,100 --> 00:07:47,020
Oh my gosh, we had practice and I squeezed.

114
00:07:47,400 --> 00:07:49,660
Oh, I'm a West team member, so you should be fine.

115
00:07:50,160 --> 00:07:50,560
Gotcha.

116
00:07:50,980 --> 00:07:52,200
Hope the East didn't rehearse.

117
00:07:52,980 --> 00:07:54,880
There's not a sporty bone in my body.

118
00:07:55,360 --> 00:07:56,720
And I have no rhythm.

119
00:07:57,420 --> 00:07:59,140
Cheering takes a toll on me.

120
00:08:01,760 --> 00:08:02,520
Never mind.

121
00:08:02,660 --> 00:08:03,720
Forget I said any of that.

122
00:08:03,720 --> 00:08:06,540
I think I'll practice a little extra before heading home.

123
00:08:07,220 --> 00:08:08,060
Right pump.

124
00:08:08,500 --> 00:08:09,820
Then left goes twice.

125
00:08:10,400 --> 00:08:11,040
Then right.

126
00:08:11,200 --> 00:08:12,460
Or was it left again?

127
00:08:12,460 --> 00:08:16,420
Um, that looks like the part both teams do.

128
00:08:16,740 --> 00:08:17,060
Yeah.

129
00:08:17,540 --> 00:08:18,180
Right first.

130
00:08:18,640 --> 00:08:18,940
Huh?

131
00:08:21,020 --> 00:08:23,940
When your right hand goes up, put your left to your chest.

132
00:08:24,300 --> 00:08:24,860
Do it with me.

133
00:08:25,520 --> 00:08:26,040
Sure.

134
00:08:27,260 --> 00:08:29,060
Next, do two pumps on the left.

135
00:08:29,500 --> 00:08:32,040
Then turn your whole body and throw a left punch.

136
00:08:32,340 --> 00:08:34,240
Oh, right, the punching part.

137
00:08:34,660 --> 00:08:37,000
Put both hands up and shakey shake shake.

138
00:08:37,660 --> 00:08:39,400
One, two, three, four.

139
00:08:40,240 --> 00:08:42,280
One, two, three, four.

140
00:08:43,120 --> 00:08:44,960
One, two, three, four.

141
00:08:45,640 --> 00:08:46,620
Great punch.

142
00:08:46,820 --> 00:08:48,920
Now let's shakey shakey shake.

143
00:08:48,920 --> 00:08:51,940
Wait, I thought those two were on opposing teams.

144
00:08:52,760 --> 00:08:54,500
I'd rather not do the cheer.

145
00:08:57,180 --> 00:08:57,660
See?

146
00:08:57,920 --> 00:08:58,920
Killing it.

147
00:08:59,480 --> 00:09:00,480
Thanks to you.

148
00:09:00,480 --> 00:09:05,840
As long as they're having fun.

149
00:09:09,840 --> 00:09:12,920
I have nothing but love for Sengoku and Remy.

150
00:09:13,920 --> 00:09:14,940
I really do.

151
00:09:15,940 --> 00:09:17,860
All you had to do was mix.

152
00:09:18,420 --> 00:09:19,800
You're mad, aren't you?

153
00:09:20,860 --> 00:09:24,720
Whatever emotion I may be processing now is entirely beside the point.

154
00:09:25,220 --> 00:09:26,480
Should Remy mix in this?

155
00:09:26,480 --> 00:09:30,280
You have to read the labels more carefully or risk botching the entire thing.

156
00:09:31,140 --> 00:09:32,380
Wait, that isn't right.

157
00:09:32,540 --> 00:09:33,420
Try this stuff here.

158
00:09:33,540 --> 00:09:33,900
No!

159
00:09:34,360 --> 00:09:37,680
Apart from reading the labels, you have to read the recipe as well, Sengoku.

160
00:09:37,680 --> 00:09:41,860
It's getting everywhere!

161
00:09:42,860 --> 00:09:46,740
Though it says salt, is it actually salt or something else?

162
00:09:46,800 --> 00:09:49,400
Most things labeled salt are going to be salt, okay?

163
00:09:49,960 --> 00:09:53,480
And why is our workstation messier than a death scene from a horror movie?

164
00:09:54,020 --> 00:09:56,860
Their group isn't done mixing in the ingredients yet?

165
00:09:57,080 --> 00:09:58,760
Class is just about over.

166
00:10:00,020 --> 00:10:01,760
Chop the veggies, Sengoku.

167
00:10:01,760 --> 00:10:03,340
You can handle that, right?

168
00:10:03,980 --> 00:10:04,380
Me?

169
00:10:04,980 --> 00:10:05,340
With...

170
00:10:05,340 --> 00:10:06,640
With weaponry?

171
00:10:08,660 --> 00:10:09,820
Kill it!

172
00:10:09,940 --> 00:10:11,500
I've slipped my mind.

173
00:10:11,820 --> 00:10:14,320
How slippery is your mind to not see the skin?

174
00:10:14,840 --> 00:10:15,920
What's Remy doing?

175
00:10:16,940 --> 00:10:18,100
Are you a killer?

176
00:10:18,640 --> 00:10:20,740
You hereby lose all knife privileges!

177
00:10:21,260 --> 00:10:23,480
Remy wants to slice up that she's two.

178
00:10:23,760 --> 00:10:25,400
Then learn how to hold kitchen knives!

179
00:10:25,720 --> 00:10:28,420
I'm gonna have nightmares about that sight for a week!

180
00:10:28,420 --> 00:10:32,520
You just stir this very carefully while I add in the ingredients.

181
00:10:32,860 --> 00:10:34,680
Nothing less and not a smidge more, okay?

182
00:10:34,960 --> 00:10:35,800
Oh, just stirring?

183
00:10:36,080 --> 00:10:36,740
Pizza cake!

184
00:10:37,220 --> 00:10:37,580
Ow!

185
00:10:38,380 --> 00:10:39,940
I cut me!

186
00:10:41,060 --> 00:10:42,400
At least it's small, though.

187
00:10:43,820 --> 00:10:46,120
Wash it with soap and then we'll get you a bandage.

188
00:10:46,260 --> 00:10:47,320
Oh, right.

189
00:10:48,080 --> 00:10:49,180
Come on, soldier.

190
00:10:49,520 --> 00:10:50,580
Let's patch you up.

191
00:10:52,140 --> 00:10:52,620
Sakura!

192
00:10:53,200 --> 00:10:53,620
Hey!

193
00:10:53,900 --> 00:10:54,840
Think this is good?

194
00:10:55,400 --> 00:10:56,360
Looks yummy!

195
00:10:56,360 --> 00:10:59,080
Time to add that stuff in.

196
00:10:59,440 --> 00:11:01,520
Wait, why is it all wibbly?

197
00:11:03,140 --> 00:11:04,500
Are you finished?

198
00:11:05,080 --> 00:11:07,320
Is it supposed to look this way?

199
00:11:07,500 --> 00:11:08,960
It's smoking like a chimney!

200
00:11:09,900 --> 00:11:11,800
Quick, we need ventilation!

201
00:11:12,260 --> 00:11:14,280
It's making my eyes stink!

202
00:11:14,700 --> 00:11:15,680
Open the windows!

203
00:11:15,680 --> 00:11:16,040
Oh!

204
00:11:19,040 --> 00:11:24,180
Even now, the memories of our last cooking class haunt me.

205
00:11:24,180 --> 00:11:29,160
Look me in the eye.

206
00:11:29,360 --> 00:11:30,380
But you're angry!

207
00:11:31,040 --> 00:11:32,340
Look at me so you understand!

208
00:11:33,140 --> 00:11:34,820
What will we be making today?

209
00:11:35,620 --> 00:11:36,100
Curry!

210
00:11:36,660 --> 00:11:37,140
Good.

211
00:11:37,640 --> 00:11:39,980
Now what ingredients did you bring?

212
00:11:40,180 --> 00:11:40,860
A radish.

213
00:11:41,200 --> 00:11:42,040
Why, though?

214
00:11:42,240 --> 00:11:42,840
Tofu?

215
00:11:43,100 --> 00:11:44,020
But why?

216
00:11:44,380 --> 00:11:47,600
Are daikon radishes included in the curry you eat at home, Sengoku?

217
00:11:48,100 --> 00:11:49,680
Well, uh, no.

218
00:11:49,860 --> 00:11:50,900
I don't believe they are.

219
00:11:51,120 --> 00:11:52,360
Then what's it doing here?

220
00:11:52,660 --> 00:11:56,380
The only time I've seen curry, it's been fully cooked in the pot and ready to go.

221
00:11:56,800 --> 00:11:59,840
Wasn't sure how to stir it, but the radish felt like a good choice.

222
00:12:00,140 --> 00:12:03,320
Any veggie you actually see in curry would have been a better choice.

223
00:12:03,320 --> 00:12:07,880
Then placing all those vegetables around the pot slowly brings forth the curry.

224
00:12:08,120 --> 00:12:09,520
No, we're cooking it!

225
00:12:09,660 --> 00:12:14,020
Our entire class lowered their standards and picked curry in hopes you would be able to do this.

226
00:12:14,400 --> 00:12:16,800
Okay, if not curry, what can you make?

227
00:12:17,060 --> 00:12:17,620
Pasta?

228
00:12:18,480 --> 00:12:19,040
Croquettes?

229
00:12:19,360 --> 00:12:24,380
The prepackaged food you simply have to unwrap and warm up doesn't qualify as a dish you make.

230
00:12:24,460 --> 00:12:25,920
I-I know that.

231
00:12:26,660 --> 00:12:30,440
Luckily, I brought stuff too, so let's start by cutting up the-

232
00:12:30,440 --> 00:12:30,900
Ah!

233
00:12:31,220 --> 00:12:32,620
Your knife privilege was revoked!

234
00:12:32,620 --> 00:12:38,020
I want you to pay very close attention to what you're doing, Sengoku.

235
00:12:39,960 --> 00:12:42,180
He-he's gotten better!

236
00:12:42,920 --> 00:12:45,620
Wow, when did you become an expert peeler, huh?

237
00:12:46,140 --> 00:12:46,960
Awesome job!

238
00:12:47,140 --> 00:12:49,200
Once peeled, we'll-

239
00:12:49,200 --> 00:12:51,620
Um, the potato disappeared.

240
00:12:52,040 --> 00:12:53,440
Cause you whittled it to nothing!

241
00:12:54,120 --> 00:12:56,120
The onion disappeared too!

242
00:12:56,300 --> 00:12:58,240
You're supposed to stop peeling at some point!

243
00:12:59,440 --> 00:13:01,700
Thank goodness our classmates saw this coming.

244
00:13:01,700 --> 00:13:05,020
All the other groups donated a portion of their curry to us.

245
00:13:05,660 --> 00:13:06,760
They know us too well.

246
00:13:07,100 --> 00:13:09,060
Sengoku will be in charge of heating the pot.

247
00:13:09,060 --> 00:13:11,180
Remy can plate the rice while we wait.

248
00:13:11,740 --> 00:13:14,460
Will dreams be the only place I went at cooking?

249
00:13:14,460 --> 00:13:18,420
Work hard enough, and those dreams will come true.

250
00:13:18,420 --> 00:13:21,200
Why in the world are the flames so high?

251
00:13:21,200 --> 00:13:23,080
High heat means high flames.

252
00:13:23,080 --> 00:13:23,880
No way!

253
00:13:23,880 --> 00:13:25,020
That was high heat?

254
00:13:25,200 --> 00:13:26,060
You lied!

255
00:13:26,060 --> 00:13:27,300
What did you do?

256
00:13:28,020 --> 00:13:28,700
Sakura?

257
00:13:28,700 --> 00:13:29,060
Sakura?

258
00:13:30,480 --> 00:13:34,000
I mean, try, but she's so sorry.

259
00:13:35,000 --> 00:13:37,860
The rice means about it and it's a girl.

260
00:13:38,540 --> 00:13:39,800
Please don't cry.

261
00:13:40,120 --> 00:13:41,160
Just let it go.

262
00:13:41,840 --> 00:13:43,820
Rice girl is fine, yeah?

263
00:13:43,820 --> 00:13:49,980
We have to eat runny rice girl with gooey curry now!

264
00:13:50,160 --> 00:13:51,600
Yes, bon appetit.

265
00:13:53,140 --> 00:13:54,800
Hey, it's pretty good.

266
00:13:55,260 --> 00:13:56,020
Isn't it, Remy?

267
00:13:56,700 --> 00:13:59,680
Yeah, wish the rice was cooked all the way, though.

268
00:14:00,180 --> 00:14:01,460
Thanks a lot for sharing.

269
00:14:01,780 --> 00:14:03,220
It's totally cool, I promise.

270
00:14:03,780 --> 00:14:05,320
Hope things turn out better next time.

271
00:14:05,320 --> 00:14:08,280
I'm sorry, again.

272
00:14:08,800 --> 00:14:09,840
Remy's a failure.

273
00:14:10,840 --> 00:14:11,660
No, you aren't.

274
00:14:11,660 --> 00:14:14,000
We all have things we don't really excel at.

275
00:14:14,680 --> 00:14:17,420
One thing you'll excel at is being someone's wife!

276
00:14:18,260 --> 00:14:21,240
Cooking isn't the only thing that makes or breaks a spouse.

277
00:14:21,580 --> 00:14:23,880
You can't deny it's definitely an advantage.

278
00:14:24,700 --> 00:14:26,160
So what should Remy do?

279
00:14:26,380 --> 00:14:28,580
No soul on earth will want to marry me.

280
00:14:28,760 --> 00:14:29,560
Me either.

281
00:14:30,000 --> 00:14:32,480
No cooking skills, no wedding rings.

282
00:14:33,480 --> 00:14:34,540
Don't you worry.

283
00:14:34,540 --> 00:14:36,580
If nobody else will have you,

284
00:14:36,860 --> 00:14:39,320
I'll take both your hands in marriage.

285
00:14:41,880 --> 00:14:42,720
No way!

286
00:14:43,120 --> 00:14:43,960
