You have to wear that.

341
00:16:40,260 --> 00:16:41,820
Well, Miyamoto, you like?

342
00:16:42,060 --> 00:16:43,040
I feel betrayed.

343
00:16:44,420 --> 00:16:46,440
Not really what I had in mind.

344
00:16:47,620 --> 00:16:49,920
Listen up, cause this can get confusing.

345
00:16:51,000 --> 00:16:54,080
In this particular sentence, this noun here gets modified.

346
00:16:54,680 --> 00:16:55,080
Got it?

347
00:16:55,080 --> 00:17:00,640
Remember, a modifying noun is more information about the...

348
00:17:00,640 --> 00:17:02,200
It's the return of the Ice Queen.

349
00:17:04,200 --> 00:17:05,300
You're with me so far?

350
00:17:06,360 --> 00:17:08,300
If so, you're looking for both seconds to...

351
00:17:08,300 --> 00:17:09,320
I hear spirits knocking.

352
00:17:10,420 --> 00:17:12,460
Now, next to read is...

353
00:17:12,460 --> 00:17:12,720
Ori.

354
00:17:16,020 --> 00:17:17,040
That's mine.

355
00:17:17,040 --> 00:17:21,380
Um, ease up on the emotion and translate it, if you please.

356
00:17:21,720 --> 00:17:23,440
Get away from her, dummy.

357
00:17:24,120 --> 00:17:26,240
And where are you pulling that from?

358
00:17:29,200 --> 00:17:31,960
I swear, she forgot her book is all.

359
00:17:32,760 --> 00:17:34,420
Yeah, so?

360
00:17:35,320 --> 00:17:37,880
So, for today, I let her share mine.

361
00:17:37,880 --> 00:17:44,940
Oh, please, no!

362
00:17:45,000 --> 00:17:46,260
What are you freaking out about?

363
00:17:46,780 --> 00:17:49,020
The fact that you're furious with me right now?

364
00:17:49,300 --> 00:17:51,900
Hey, you're afraid when I haven't said a word?

365
00:17:52,960 --> 00:17:54,900
I'm not hiding anything at all, Ori.

366
00:17:55,440 --> 00:17:56,740
